{"id":4816,"date":"2018-06-09T13:15:35","date_gmt":"2018-06-09T17:15:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=4816"},"modified":"2018-06-09T13:15:35","modified_gmt":"2018-06-09T17:15:35","slug":"our-visit-to-the-voice-of-america","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2018\/06\/09\/our-visit-to-the-voice-of-america\/","title":{"rendered":"Our Visit to the &#8220;Voice Of America&#8221;"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>One of the benefits of attending the Dayton Amateur Radio Association &#8220;HamVention&#8221; every year is to spend time with my long-time (notice I didn&#8217;t say &#8220;old&#8221;) friends.\u00a0 Dave, Ed, and I grew up together in the 60&#8217;s in Redford Township, Michigan &#8211; a western suburb of Detroit.\u00a0 We played together, we rode bikes together, we got in trouble together and we attended school together (since the 2nd grade) and we also got our ham radio licenses together &#8211; all first licensed in 1969.<\/p>\n<p>This year at HamVention we decided we&#8217;d like to take a trip away from the main venue and visit the site of the Bethany Transmitting Station of the world famous Voice Of America (VOA) located just off I-75 between Dayton and Cincinnati.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_4818\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4818\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200220.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-4818 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200220.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200220.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200220-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200220-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200220-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-4818\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">VOA Bethany Transmitting Station<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>The VOA Bethany Relay Station was designed by the Crosley Broadcasting Corporation.\u00a0 Although the actual recording studios were in New York City and later moved to Washington, D.C., the signals were relayed through dedicated AT&amp;T long distance telephone lines to the transmitter site near Cincinnati.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_184035.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4819\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_184035.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_184035.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_184035-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_184035-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_184035-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>The VOA began in 1942 as a radio program designed to explain America\u2019s policies during\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.history.com\/topics\/world-war-ii\" data-type=\"topics\" data-id=\"142543\">World War II<\/a>\u00a0and to bolster the morale of its allies throughout Europe, Asia, the Middle East, and Africa. After the war, VOA continued as part of America\u2019s Cold War propaganda arsenal and was primarily directed toward the western European audience. In February 1947, VOA began its first Russian-language broadcasts into the Soviet Union.<\/p>\n<p>With the words, \u201cHello! This is\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.history.com\/topics\/us-states\/new-york\" data-type=\"topics\" data-id=\"144006\">New York<\/a>\u00a0calling,\u201d the U.S. Voice of America (VOA) begins its first radio broadcasts to the\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.history.com\/topics\/history-of-the-soviet-union\" data-type=\"topics\" data-id=\"195520\">Soviet Union<\/a>. The VOA effort was an important part of America\u2019s propaganda campaign against the Soviet Union during the\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.history.com\/topics\/cold-war\" data-type=\"topics\" data-id=\"142555\">Cold War<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>The initial broadcast explained that VOA was going to \u201cgive listeners in the USSR a picture of life in America.\u201d News stories, human-interest features, and music comprised the bulk of the programming. The purpose was to give the Russian audience the \u201cpure and unadulterated truth\u201d about life outside the USSR. Voice of America hoped that this would \u201cbroaden the bases of understanding and friendship between the Russian and American people.\u201d<\/p>\n<p>The Bethany site encompassed hundreds of acres of land for the huge rhombic antenna farm that could be switched to direct the 1.2 million watts of radio frequency programming to different locations around the world, depending on the time of day and atmospheric conditions.<\/p>\n<div id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-4816 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-full'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190636.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190636.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4820\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190636.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190636-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190636-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190636-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4820'>\n\t\t\t\tThe main transmitter control room\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191327.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191327.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4821\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191327.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191327-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191327-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191327-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4821'>\n\t\t\t\tOne of the large switching systems for the various transmitters \n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191703.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191703.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4822\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191703.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191703-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191703-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191703-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4822'>\n\t\t\t\tThe room where the electric power came into the transmitting building\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192207.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"304\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192207.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4823\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4823'>\n\t\t\t\tOne of the six transmitting tubes that created the 1.2 million watts of RF\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192516.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192516.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-4824\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192516.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192516-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192516-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192516-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-4824'>\n\t\t\t\tThe base of the antenna switch network out in the field\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\n<p>In one of the pictures above you can see my friend Dave talking to the last remaining employee of the VOA at this site &#8212; Dave&#8217;s getting quite a history lesson.<\/p>\n<p>Note the windows at the top of the tower in the first picture &#8211; It kind of looks like an airport control tower.\u00a0 I asked our tour guide the purpose of that tower.\u00a0 His response &#8230; &#8220;for sharpshooters&#8221;.\u00a0 This Bethany Relay Station was specifically placed here because of it&#8217;s distance from the east coast stations where they could be more susceptible to enemy attack.\u00a0 Even though the Bethany Station was so far west, they still stationed military armed personnel to protect the Voice Of America to make sure the message always got out.<\/p>\n<p>Due to new satellite and internet technology, the need for the high power RF radio broadcast stations has diminished and the station was closed as an active transmitting site in 1994.\u00a0 Fear not however as the Voice Of America still broadcasts every day from their studios in Washington D.C. and their programming can be heard on the internet and on some local PBS network stations around the country.\u00a0 Find out more and listen to VOA live at\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.voanews.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https:\/\/www.voanews.com\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>And thanks to dedicated volunteers, we were able to tour the museum.\u00a0 Take a look at the pictures below.<\/p>\n<div id='gallery-2' class='gallery galleryid-4816 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-full'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_185210.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_185210.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4830\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_185210.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_185210-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_185210-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_185210-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4830'>\n\t\t\t\tA 40&#8217;s vintage Crosley convertible\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190007.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190007.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4831\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190007.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190007-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190007-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190007-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4831'>\n\t\t\t\tOne of the ham radio club operating stations\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190015.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190015.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4832\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190015.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190015-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190015-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190015-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4832'>\n\t\t\t\tAnother ham radio operating station\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190803.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190803.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4833\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190803.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190803-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190803-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_190803-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4833'>\n\t\t\t\tEarly ham radio equipment by the R.L. Drake Company of Miamisburg, OH\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191656.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191656.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4834\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191656.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191656-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191656-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191656-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4834'>\n\t\t\t\tPart of Robert L. Drake&#8217;s personal ham radio collection\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191934.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191934.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4835\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191934.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191934-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191934-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_191934-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4835'>\n\t\t\t\tSome of the early Crosley Co. products on display in the museum\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192049.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192049.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4836\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192049.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192049-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192049-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192049-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4836'>\n\t\t\t\tMore Crosley Co. products\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192624.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192624.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4837\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192624.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192624-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192624-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_192624-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4837'>\n\t\t\t\tView from the rear of the VOA Bethany Station\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_193351.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_193351.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4838\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_193351.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_193351-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_193351-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_193351-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4838'>\n\t\t\t\tMy Grandson Garret learning about early radio communications\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200054.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200054.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-2-4839\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200054.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200054-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200054-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/06\/20180518_200054-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-2-4839'>\n\t\t\t\tFront lobby of VOA &#8211; my buddy Dave in the foreground and Ed at the top of the stairs.\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\n<p>Here&#8217;s a few pix of us boys at the Dayton HamVention and at the VOA<\/p>\n<div id='gallery-3' class='galle